{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,320p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md && rg -n 'cljd|cljs|node-tests|cljstyle|kondo|debruijn-register|register' deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn package.json Makefile bin test src 2>/dev/null | head -300\"","aggregated_output":"---\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\nbb test              # Run all tests (JVM, Node/CLJS, Dart/CLJD)\nbb test:clj          # JVM tests only (or: clj -M:test)\nbb test:cljs         # ClojureScript / Node tests (via shadow-cljs :cljs alias)\nbb test:cljd         # ClojureDart tests (requires flutter on PATH)\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\n\n# ClojureScript / shadow-cljs (always via deps.edn :cljs alias, never npx)\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch <build-id>    # e.g. watch demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build-id>  # e.g. compile demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release <build-id>  # production release\n\n# ClojureDart\nclj -M:cljd compile\n\n# Linting\nclj -M:kondo --lint <path>\n```\n\n`bb test:cljd`'s `dart test` globs everything under `test/cljd-out/`,\nwhich the cljd compile does not prune when a source file is deleted or\nrenamed. A stale compiled `.dart` test for an already-deleted namespace\ncan silently pass, giving a false-clean run. Run `rm -rf test/cljd-out`\nbefore any `bb test:cljd` you're relying on to prove a deletion (or\nsimilar rename/removal) actually took effect.\n\n## Testing Philosophy & TDD\n\nWrite tests before implementing features (TDD).\n\nTests define the contract and expected behavior. Implementation follows from the tests, not the other way around.\n\nWhen implementing a feature or fix:\n1. **Red phase**: Write the test first — define what should happen.\n2. **Green phase**: Implement the minimum code to pass the test.\n3. **Refactor phase**: Refactor if needed while keeping tests green.\n\nThis ensures code is testable by design and implementation matches actual requirements.\n\n## Debugging Malformed CLJ / EDN / CLJS\n\nA single missing bracket can silently break an entire file. The compiler may still succeed, with subsequent forms nesting inside the broken one.\n\n1. **Run clj-kondo first**:\n   ```sh\n   clj -M:kondo --lint path/to/file.cljs\n   ```\n\n2. **If clj-kondo reports a mismatch, write a bracket-tracing script**:\n   Do NOT try to eyeball-count brackets. Track a stack of `(char, line, col)` for every opener. Handle: string literals, escaped chars, and `;;` line comments.\n\n3. **Fix one bracket at a time, re-run checker after each fix**:\n   Common patterns:\n   - Hiccup vector missing `]` causes siblings to become extra arguments.\n   - `defn`/`let` missing `)` causes subsequent top-level forms to nest inside.\n   - Both can coexist while total bracket count is zero-sum.\n\n4. **After brackets balance**, rerun `clj-kondo`, then rebuild with `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build>`.\npackage.json:6:    \"shadow-cljs\": \"3.3.5\"\nshadow-cljs.edn:1:;; shadow-cljs configuration\nshadow-cljs.edn:2:;; Source paths come from deps.edn (:paths plus the :cljs alias's\nshadow-cljs.edn:5:{:deps {:aliases [:cljs]}\nshadow-cljs.edn:19:                 :output-to \"target/node-tests.js\"\nbb.edn:5:  test:cljs {:doc \"Run Node tests (via shadow-cljs with :cljs alias)\"\nbb.edn:6:             :task (shell \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile slice-peer test\")}\nbb.edn:11:   ;; namespace, and this project's cljd.core carries the Flutter extensions,\nbb.edn:14:   ;; cljd-out tree, so a peer built after it would import a tree it does\nbb.edn:17:             (shell \"clojure -M:cljd compile dao.stream.slice-peer\")\nbb.edn:18:             (shell \"dart compile exe lib/cljd-out/dao/stream/slice-peer.dart -o build/slice-peer\"))}\nbb.edn:24:   ;; builds it first; a bare `bb test:clj` or `bb test:cljs` without it\nbb.edn:27:             (shell \"clojure -M:cljd compile yin.repl.slice-peer\")\nbb.edn:28:             (shell \"dart compile exe lib/cljd-out/yin/repl/slice-peer.dart -o build/yin-repl-peer\"))}\nbb.edn:30:  test:cljd {:doc \"Run Dart tests (via clojure -M:cljd)\"\nbb.edn:32:             :task (shell \"clojure -M:cljd test\")}\nbb.edn:35:        :depends [build:yin-repl-peer test:clj test:cljs test:cljd]}}}\ndeps.edn:16: :cljd/opts {}\ndeps.edn:17: :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"]\ndeps.edn:33:           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\ndeps.edn:34:                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\ndeps.edn:36:                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\ndeps.edn:38:                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\ndeps.edn:41:                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\ndeps.edn:48:           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\ndeps.edn:52:                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\ndeps.edn:53:                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\ndeps.edn:58:           :cljs-yin-repl\ndeps.edn:60:            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\ndeps.edn:62:                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\ndeps.edn:63:            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\" \"run\" \"yin.repl/-main\"]}\ndeps.edn:66:           :kondo {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version \"2026.01.19\"}}\ndeps.edn:67:                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"clj-kondo.main\"]}\ndeps.edn:69:                 :main-opts [\"-m\" \"debug-cljd\"]\ndeps.edn:70:                 :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\ndeps.edn:71:           :cljd-yin-repl\ndeps.edn:76:           :cljd-yin-repl-build\ndeps.edn:80:    